Subject: [PATCH 23/78] PlaitOS: app downgrade switch turns itself off

plait_pm_downgrade_allowed is meant for a one-off install, so it doesn't stay on:
- once a downgrade gets past the version check because of it
- an hour after it was switched on
- at boot (the hour can't be measured across a reboot)

PlaitDowngradeTimeout watches the setting from PackageManagerService.systemReady()
and does the writes on the package handler, never under mPm.mLock.

